#B2. Discover 5 unique strong security implementations.

1. Passwordless hardware authentication, WebAuthn
Using WebAuthn to replace traditional passwords or SMS multi-factor authentication
Why is it strong?
It is immune to credential stuffing and phishing attack. The private key will never leave the secure enclave of the harden token. 
Also the process relies on verifying a digital signature server-side. Even if a user is tricked to visit a replica website, the browser will refuse to sign the challenge because the domine name is not match.

2. Zero trust architecture via micro-segmentation
Instead of network boundary model, it divids the network and isolated zones into individual containers.
Why is it strong?
It always verify instead of 'trust'. Traditionally, when attacker gains access to local network, he can freely compromise other machines, 
while micro-segmentation ensures a strict firewall rules, identity checks and encrypted communication channel between resources.
If a single web server is compromised, the attacker will be locked inside a segment and not be able to pivot to the backend database or internal directory.

3. Argon2id
It can be used as the primary algorithm for hashing user credentials or deriving encryption keys from master passwords.
Why is it strong?
Traditional hashing function, like SHA-256, is easy to be brute-force by ASICs or GPU arrays. 
Argon2id forces the system to dedicate a customize amount of RAM that creates an asymmentric disadvantage for attackers that he had to run billions of guesses simultaneously while legit server only takes a second.

4. strict CSP (content security policy) with cryptographic nonces
It applies a unique nonce into a legitimate scripts while deploying a restrictive http response header.
Why is it strong?
It it able to defense against XSS as if an attacker injects a ma;ocopis payload into a database string, the browser will refuse to execute it.
The attacker will not able to guess the the secure random value that generated by the server for that specific page load while the mailicious script will remains dead and lost in the DOM

5. Automated secrets management
While using dynamic short-lived tokens by injecting them at runtime using a secrets manager, this can eliminate hardcoded configuration credentials, API tokens and database password.
Why is it strong?
This remove the credential leakage risk with Github repositories or compromised workstations. 
Presenting a secure cryptographic identity token to the secrets manager, then it will generate a unique and temporary database user with restricted permission that will be expired and destroy after a short period of time.
It will become useless when an attacker tries to exfiltrate an active token.
